  "Shared parity fixture for the guarded CI-config path matcher (issue #2865).",
  "Read by the agent test (agent/test/ci-config-guard-raw.test.ts) and by the Go port in api/internal/pushbroker; both must agree on every entry.",
  "Semantics: globs are server-trusted and trimmed (empty/blank ones dropped); file paths are matched RAW (no trim, no normalisation, a fully empty path is ignored).",
  "'**/' = optional run of any characters ending in '/', '**' = any characters, '*' = any characters except '/'; 'any' includes newlines. Anchored on the whole path.",
  "cases[]: {name, globs, path, match}: path matches iff it matches ANY glob.",
  "changeSets[]: {name, globs, changed, flagged}: flagged is the de-duplicated, input-ordered subset of changed that matches, byte-exact.",
  "String data only: control and non-ASCII characters are JSON escapes; no real CI file is ever written."
